{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774302607,"nonce":"tABLrdQ8+BZG9oM7g7AJQtXm79w=","title":"dev-browser tool unavailable to subagents","message":"When spawning subagents via the Agent tool, dev-browser is not available as a tool. The subagent receives WebFetch (which cannot render SPAs or interact with JavaScript) but not the browser automation capability.\n\nThis means browser verification workflows must be done by the top-level agent directly rather than delegated. For complex bigbuild workflows where the orchestrating agent wants to delegate browser testing to a verification subagent, this is a significant limitation.\n\n**Expected behavior**: Subagents should be able to use dev-browser (or a similar tool) for browser automation, at least when the parent agent explicitly grants it.\n\n**Workaround**: The top-level agent must perform browser testing itself rather than delegating.","files":null}]}